{"kind":"assert","text":"Item 4 exact head 28e1146b has two coupled seat-authority defects. First, foldJoin excludes only the creator's exact actor key, so two chess-scoped keys resolving at their record positions to the same persistent identity may occupy both colors; foldMove then authorizes each side independently and lets that identity move both colors. Second, sameSeat upgrades an unanchored seat to persistent identity before the enclosing move/draw act passes all legality guards, so a rejected act can silently change later authority. Repair must reject persistent-identity seat collision, make identity matching pure until the act is effective, commit any seat upgrade only after all guards pass, and add mutation-sensitive regressions for same-identity join/move and ineffective-act non-upgrade.","body":{"head":"28e1146b068d4f489e5478cc6e045cf5f8edecc2","scope":"item-4-seat-authority","severity":"security"}}